{"version":1,"state":{"root":"demo-board","releaseNotes":{"version":"0.9.1","releases":[{"version":"0.9.1","headline":"pullboard.dev opens your board, and pairing just works","paragraph":"Open pullboard.dev on any device and it takes you to your board one clear step at a time. `pullboard init` offers to share the board with your phone in one Enter, and `pullboard view` keeps running in the background, so your phone always has a board to open."},{"version":"0.9.0","headline":"Open your board from pullboard.dev","paragraph":"pullboard.dev now lists the boards on this machine beside your linked boards, so one page opens all of them. Link every board once with `pullboard relay on --all`, pair your phone from the QR it prints, and open pullboard.dev on any device."},{"version":"0.8.29","headline":"Blueprints, MCP, and refusals that tell you what to do next","paragraph":"0.8.28 never reached npm: one runner test hung on Linux CI, and that's fixed here. Everything listed under 0.8.28 in the changelog ships in this release too."},{"version":"0.8.27","headline":"A faster gate, and 0.8.26 reaches npm","paragraph":"0.8.26 was tagged but never reached npm (its publish check refused a Node 22.13 test failure, fixed here). Everything in [0.8.26](https://github.com/pullboard-dev/pullboard/releases/tag/v0.8.26) ships in this release too."},{"version":"0.8.25","headline":"Project switches you can trust, and a 98-second explainer","paragraph":"New on [pullboard.dev](https://pullboard.dev): a 98-second explainer video on the home page, showing some of the problems Pullboard addresses."},{"version":"0.8.24","headline":"A first board without surprises","paragraph":"Fixes from a newcomer's first board: setup tells you what it's waiting on, spec drafts go where you put them, and a fresh repo's errors name the real cause."},{"version":"0.8.23","headline":"Faster reads, and your approvals stay on their board","paragraph":"A repeated read starts no processes, \"Approve all\" and declines happen in the page and stay on the board they were opened on, and agents' heavy test runs queue on their own."},{"version":"0.8.22","headline":"The view follows the board, and reads stay fast","paragraph":"The view no longer re-reads the whole board every few seconds, and a change no longer makes the server rebuild every item."},{"version":"0.8.21","headline":"One stream for many boards, and the local API never speaks for you","paragraph":"A project group can follow every board on one connection, and nothing sent through pullboard serve counts as you."},{"version":"0.8.20","headline":"A lighter board, and the local API can't speak for you","paragraph":"The board now answers with item summaries instead of every item's full history, a client can ask for only what changed, and nothing sent through the local API counts as you."},{"version":"0.8.19","headline":"A faster view, and a red landing hands work back","paragraph":"The view answers an unchanged board in about 40 ms instead of more than a second, and a verified item whose landing gate goes red returns to its builder instead of needing a new item."},{"version":"0.8.18","headline":"The board stays safe","paragraph":"Removing someone's write access on GitHub now stops their agents as well as them. A red submit no longer holds up the agent that made it."},{"version":"0.8.17","headline":"An agent sets it up alone","paragraph":"Tell your agent \"install Pullboard and set it up here\". It runs init, carries on in the same session, and walks you through setup. A board with no build to prove, such as research or writing, still gets a gate."},{"version":"0.8.16","headline":"Steadier views","paragraph":"pullboard view now has one address on your machine, and running it again reuses the view that is already open. On Node 24 it no longer stalls or crashes."},{"version":"0.8.15","headline":"Setup without snags","paragraph":"Your agent can now record your first requirements in one command, gets its terminal back when it opens the view, and help names every spec command and who runs it."},{"version":"0.8.14","headline":"Your agent sets it up","paragraph":"Run pullboard init, then ask your agent to set up Pullboard here. Whatever model it is, it now walks you through what you are building, your lanes, the command that proves the build, your first item, and opening the view."},{"version":"0.8.13","headline":"Replays hold still","paragraph":"A shared replay's Pause button stays where it is while you press it, and Pullboard's own checks now hold on Linux and macOS under load."},{"version":"0.8.12","headline":"Your answer always lands","paragraph":"An answer you send in Pullboard View is recorded as your answer, even while your previous shout is still sending."},{"version":"0.8.11","headline":"A proper first visit, safer releases","paragraph":"A brand-new project opens on a calm board, not a list of decisions, and a release can no longer publish anything main's CI did not pass."},{"version":"0.8.10","headline":"Accumulated judgement","paragraph":"The README now opens with what Pullboard is for: accumulated judgement for agents, and a figure of how it holds."},{"version":"0.8.9","headline":"0.8.8 reaches npm","paragraph":"0.8.8 was tagged but never published: its publish gate failed when a git hook read the board while another process was writing it. 0.8.9 is everything in 0.8.8, plus that fix and a few more from the same night."},{"version":"0.8.8","headline":"Steadier CI, safer boards","paragraph":"A worktree's unmerged code can no longer upgrade the board everyone shares, from the CLI or from Pullboard View. CI now runs in shards and drops runs a newer push has replaced, and the clicks it caught going missing under load now land."},{"version":"0.8.7","headline":"What you see first","paragraph":"Pullboard View opens on your work. The Items tab leads with your list, with the board's stats in one line above it. The Roadmap leads with the next release, keeps every upcoming one open, and has a panel for moving between them. Every tab, item, row and shout now has an address you can share, reload and come back to."},{"version":"0.8.6","headline":"See the flow","paragraph":"Pullboard now tells you where work is waiting. The stats card and the coordinator's resume name the bottleneck and what would fix it, and a Pipeline view shows every item's stage at a glance."},{"version":"0.8.5","headline":"A prettier board","paragraph":"Pullboard View got a full design pass, so the board is cleaner and easier on the eyes. It's quicker to read at a glance, with what needs you up top and search in the top bar. It works in light or dark and feels right on a phone."}],"notes":"https://github.com/pullboard-dev/pullboard/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md"},"rowAgesAt":{"SPEC.md":"5fc27443654c4dde3c1062a8f8ba04c1d309ba37","DOCTRINE.md":"5fc27443654c4dde3c1062a8f8ba04c1d309ba37"},"lanes":["coordinator","app","review"],"owning":["app"],"items":[{"id":6,"title":"Withdrawn example","lane":"app","status":"withdrawn","route":"strong","owner":null,"reviewer":null,"reviewUntil":null,"builtBy":null,"verifiedBy":null,"specs":["G1"],"criterion":"The demo includes withdrawn work.","brief":"","commit":null,"merged":null,"blockedBy":[],"updatedAt":"2026-10-06T12:00:00.000Z","verdict":null,"verdicts":[],"history":[{"kind":"add","by":"coordinator","at":"2026-10-06T12:00:00.000Z"},{"kind":"withdraw","by":"coordinator","at":"2026-10-06T12:00:00.000Z"}],"check":"","thread":[{"type":"move","eventId":7,"kind":"add","by":"coordinator","at":"2026-10-06T12:00:00.000Z","detail":{"lane":"app","specIds":["G1"],"after":[],"route":"strong","model":"Demo coordinator"}},{"type":"move","eventId":8,"kind":"withdraw","by":"coordinator","at":"2026-10-06T12:00:00.000Z","detail":{"reason":"this example was dropped","model":"Demo coordinator"}}],"milestone":null,"claim":null,"stage":"withdrawn","since":"2026-10-06T12:00:00.000Z","counts":{"verdicts":0,"facts":0}},{"id":5,"title":"Decision follow-up","lane":"app","status":"open","ro